  "description": "ULETEM crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C120 H232 Gd6 N6 Ni8 O60,x(C1 H4 O1),y(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Ni1 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni3 (Ni) has 6 O neighbors; Ni4 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Ni1B (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni2B (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni3B (Ni) has 6 O neighbors; Ni4B (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Gd1B (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2B (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3B (Gd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 25 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.034-4.076 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 91.08-131.98°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C120H232Gd6N6Ni8O60. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 16 Piv (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
